./canon/drops/20260907/extracted/text/doc0_governance_architecture.txt:464:[P style=''] This document is the layer every other Akki specification instantiates. A new engine specification names which of the twelve attributes it serves. A new rule, under rule_criteria_spec_v1, is classified against Part 1's definitions before it is assigned a domain. A new component is added to Part 2 with build requirements derived the same way the sixteen above were derived — cited to the attribute and clause they come from, not restated as a generic obligation. A new gap, found after ratification, is added to Part 3 in the same two-section form: named in Section 1, specified in full in Section 2.
